    "body": "> Reviewed commit: `df85c092067d1ddcedabe6234e13a7cdc73c5f73`\n\nThe provided diff indicates the deletion of a TypeScript build cache file (`.cache/.tsbuildinfo-typecheck`) and a Playwright Visual Regression Test (VRT) snapshot (`tests/playwright/vrt-connect-page.spec.ts-snapshots/connect-page-scanning-chromium-linux.png`).\n\nWhile deleting build cache is a standard practice, the removal of a VRT snapshot, especially in a PR focused on UI optimization, raises a significant concern. The PR description mentions \"Optimize Timer and HR Tiles for Vertical Space Density\" and states \"7 files, ~417 lines\" of changes. However, the provided diff only shows deletions of cache and a single VRT snapshot, which does not align with the described scope or line count. This suggests either the diff provided for review is incomplete, or the PR's description is misleading relative to the actual changes.\n\nRegarding the VRT snapshot deletion:\n`tests/playwright/vrt-connect-page.spec.ts-snapshots/connect-page-scanning-chromium-linux.png`\n\nIf UI changes were made, new VRT snapshots should be generated and committed to reflect the new visual state, rather than deleting existing ones without replacement. Deleting a snapshot for a `connect-page` when the PR is about 'Timer and HR Tiles' also suggests a potential disconnect or an unintended side effect. This could lead to visual regressions going unnoticed for the `connect-page` in the future, which violates the principles outlined in `docs/DESIGN_GUIDELINES.md` regarding Automated Accessibility Testing and preventing regressions.\n\nPlease clarify the full scope of changes in this PR and ensure that all relevant VRT snapshots are updated or added as necessary, especially if UI elements have been modified. If the `connect-page` was not affected, the deletion should be justified.\n\n> Reviewed at commit: `df85c092067d1ddcedabe6234e13a7cdc73c5f73`\n",
