    "body": "> Reviewed commit: `aa1f60ade12ce29139d30355c8b9af23aeb55fcb`\n\nThe provided diff is heavily truncated and primarily shows the deletion of build cache files (`.cache/.tsbuildinfo-typecheck`) and Playwright visual regression test snapshots. While removing build artifacts from version control is a good practice, and updating VRT snapshots is expected, the core changes related to the 'Optimize Timer and HR Tiles for Vertical Space Density' feature (as indicated by the PR title) are not visible in this diff.\n\nGiven the PR context states '~417 lines' of changes, it's highly probable that the actual feature implementation is missing from the provided diff. Without the full code changes, a proper review of the feature cannot be conducted.\n\n**Visible Changes**:\n*   **Deletion of `.cache/.tsbuildinfo-typecheck`**: This is a positive change. Build artifacts should not be committed to version control.\n*   **Deletion of Playwright VRT snapshots**: This is typically part of updating visual tests, which is acceptable.\n\n**Concern regarding PR Scope**:\nThe PR title indicates a feature (`feat(medium): Optimize Timer and HR Tiles...`), but the visible diff is entirely related to cleanup and test updates. If the actual feature changes are also part of this PR, it violates the 'One Logical Change Per PR' guideline as stated in `docs/DEVELOPMENT.md` (Pull Request (PR) Process -> PR Scope). It's crucial for PRs to be tightly scoped to ensure efficient and focused reviews.\n\nPlease provide the complete diff for the feature implementation or split this PR into separate, tightly-scoped PRs (one for cleanup/test updates, one for the feature).\n\n> Reviewed at commit: `aa1f60ade12ce29139d30355c8b9af23aeb55fcb`\n",
