    "body": "### \ud83e\udd16 AI Technical Audit\n\n## Code Review: PR #8882 - Optimize Timer and HR Tiles\n\n### \ud83d\udee1\ufe0f ANTI-AI-SLOP DIRECTIVES\n\n1.  **OVER-ENGINEERING (Major):** \n    *   **Problem:** In `TimerDisplay.tsx`, you have implemented a custom SVG `ProgressRing` component (~40 lines). This is unnecessary maintenance overhead.\n    *   **Fix:** Use Material UI's existing `<CircularProgress variant=\"determinate\" />`. It supports custom size, thickness, and colors via the `sx` prop, doing exactly what your custom SVG does but with better theme integration and less code.\n2.  **CODE RATIO (Deletion Target > 40 lines):**\n    *   **Target:** `AnimatedCounter` in `TimerDisplay.tsx`.\n    *   **Reason:** This component strictly wraps a `Typography` element with style props. It creates an unnecessary abstraction layer. Passing the `sx` props directly to the `Typography` in the render body is cleaner and reduces the component count.\n    *   **Target:** `TimerDisplay.tsx` comments like `// PREPARE: Show countdown seconds only` or `// STOPWATCH: Show elapsed time MM:SS`. The code logic `if (currentPhase === 'PREPARE')` is self-explanatory. Delete these comments.\n3.  **STALE FEATURES:**\n    *   Good job removing `IdentityTier`, `HeroTier`, etc., in `HrTile.tsx`. The cleanup is verified.\n\n---\n\n### File-by-File Analysis\n\n#### `components/TimerDisplay.tsx`\n\n**1. Re-inventing the Wheel (ProgressRing)**\nInstead of the custom SVG implementation, use the library component.\n\n*Implementation Sample (Replacement):*\n```tsx\n// DELETE: const ProgressRing = ...\n\n// USE:\n<CircularProgress\n  variant=\"determinate\"\n  value={progressPercentage}\n  size={100}\n  thickness={4}\n  sx={{ \n    color: phaseColor,\n    '& .MuiCircularProgress-circle': {\n      strokeLinecap: 'round',\n    }\n  }}\n/>\n```\n\n**2. Performance & Rendering**\n*   **Issue:** The `textShadow` on the timer (`0 0 20px ${phaseColor}80`) is expensive to repaint every second (or more frequently) on lower-end mobile devices. \n*   **Recommendation:** Verify performance on mobile. If jitter occurs, consider removing the shadow or ensuring `will-change: contents` is applied.\n\n#### `components/HrTile.tsx`\n\n**1. Testability Risk (VRT)**\n*   **Problem:** In `tests/playwright/vrt-connect-page.spec.ts`, you changed the mask to `connectPage.getByTestId('hr-tile-card')`. However, in `HrTile.tsx`, I do not see `data-testid=\"hr-tile-card\"` explicitly added to the root `ControlCard`. Unless `ControlCard` has this hardcoded or receives it via `...props` *and* the parent passes it, this test selector will fail or select nothing.\n*   **Action:** Explicitly add `data-testid=\"hr-tile-card\"` to the `ControlCard` in `HrTile.tsx` to ensure stability.\n\n**2. Hardcoded Values**\n*   **Problem:** `minHeight: { xs: 110, md: 130 }` and `bgcolor: 'rgba(255,255,255,0.1)'`.\n*   **Recommendation:** Use theme spacing (e.g., `theme.spacing(14)`) and theme palette alpha helpers (e.g., `alpha(theme.palette.common.white, 0.1)`) for consistency.\n\n#### `components/HrmConnectionPanel.tsx`\n\n**1. Responsive Grid Logic**\n*   **Observation:** `gridTemplateColumns: { xs: '1fr 1fr', ... }` forces two columns even on very narrow devices (e.g., iPhone SE, Galaxy Fold cover). \n*   **Recommendation:** Consider `repeat(auto-fit, minmax(140px, 1fr))` for `xs` as well, or ensure the `HrTile` content handles sub-150px widths gracefully without overflow.\n\n### Summary\nThe architectural shift to a responsive grid is excellent. The main requirement for approval is removing the custom SVG implementation in `TimerDisplay` to reduce technical debt.\n\n*Review automatically published via RepoAuditor.*",
